WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.632
On this slide, we are focusing on avoid leakage.

00:00:03.632 --> 00:00:08.287
Start with the meaning of the idea before worrying about the exact syntax.

00:00:08.287 --> 00:00:14.317
Ask what information is going in, what Python is doing with it, and what result should come out.

00:00:14.317 --> 00:00:19.827
Leakage happens when training uses information that would not be available at prediction time.

00:00:19.827 --> 00:00:23.477
It can make evaluation look unrealistically strong.

00:00:23.477 --> 00:00:27.272
Machine learning is a workflow rather than a single fit command.

00:00:27.272 --> 00:00:32.757
Keep training information separate from evaluation data, compare against a baseline,

00:00:32.757 --> 00:00:37.227
and interpret model performance in the context of the real prediction problem.

00:00:37.227 --> 00:00:42.982
Before moving on, explain the main idea in one sentence without reading the slide.

00:00:42.982 --> 00:00:48.402
That quick explanation is a useful check that the concept is becoming reusable knowledge.
